  "query_preview": "..\nA seasonal trade-wind regime is expected to continue across the \nMarianas through at least this weekend, as the trade-wind surge \nbuilds due to an increasing pressure gradient between the tropics and\nthe midlatitudes. This trade-wind surge is strong enough to keep the\ndescending shearline from intruding into the region, pushing it out \nmore west of 140E and moreso toward the Philippines. As such, only \nisolated to low-end scattered showers are expected the next several \ndays, staying mostly dry for much of next week. As we delve further\ninto the season and winter settles across east Asia, shearlines are\nexpected to descend further into the tropics over the coming months,\nwhich may bring periods of refreshing, albeit windier conditions.",
